UID:rosh-hashanah-20271002@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271003
SUMMARY:Rosh Hashanah
DESCRIPTION:Rosh Hashanah is the Jewish New Year\, observed on the first an
 d second days of Tishri and beginning at sunset the evening before the dat
 e a civil calendar shows. It opens the ten days of repentance that close w
 ith Yom Kippur\, and it falls in the seventh month of the Hebrew calendar 
 rather than the first. The Torah commands the day but never calls it a new
  year\; the name\, and the idea\, belong to the rabbis who compiled the Mi
 shnah.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/rosh-hashanah/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/rosh-hashanah/
CATEGORIES:Celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
